      CPO ANSWER (AskUserQuestion, 2026-06-13): "Pin + remove dead" — pin the used dep (requests==2.33.1), DROP the two unused deps (beautifulsoup4 AND pandas) and the redundant root functions-framework, leave pyarrow + the floor-pinned deps untouched (out of F20 scope). The pandas removal — NOT named in F20's text — was explicitly stated in the question context ("beautifulsoup4 + pandas have zero usage anywhere") and in the chosen option's description ("DROP unused (beautifulsoup4, pandas)"); the CPO approved it knowingly.
  (2) PR structure for #425 + #427.
      CPO ANSWER (AskUserQuestion, 2026-06-13): two separate PRs (#425 deps, #427 data-contract docs) — independent, different reviewer routings, independent merge.
